1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,557
F S L info and F S L stats.

2
00:00:03,557 --> 00:00:06,719
Inspect image metadata and compute targeted summary statistics.

3
00:00:06,719 --> 00:00:11,067
The goal is clear: Choose F S L info for metadata.

4
00:00:11,917 --> 00:00:15,578
Metadata describes the container; statistics describe its values.

5
00:00:15,578 --> 00:00:21,528
F S L info reports header fields such as dimensions and voxel sizes.

6
00:00:21,528 --> 00:00:28,393
F S L stats computes statistics over image intensities, optionally after applying thresholds or masks.

7
00:00:28,393 --> 00:00:34,343
A number is only interpretable when you know which voxels contributed to it.

8
00:00:34,343 --> 00:00:40,293
For example, F S L stats image -R reports the robust intensity range.

9
00:00:40,293 --> 00:00:44,870
-V reports the number and physical volume of nonzero voxels.

10
00:00:44,870 --> 00:00:52,193
Nonzero voxels are not automatically the brain; background noise, skull, or artifacts may also be nonzero.

11
00:00:53,043 --> 00:00:56,167
Now connect the idea to an observable check.

12
00:00:56,167 --> 00:01:00,071
First, run F S L info and record image dimensions.

13
00:01:00,071 --> 00:01:04,366
Next, use F S L stats -R for the intensity range.

14
00:01:04,366 --> 00:01:07,490
Then, use -V and explain both returned numbers.

15
00:01:07,490 --> 00:01:11,395
After that, open the image to verify what was counted.

16
00:01:11,395 --> 00:01:14,518
The command shown on screen is an example.

17
00:01:14,518 --> 00:01:20,375
Adapt its path to your own working directory and verify the target before running it.

18
00:01:21,225 --> 00:01:23,276
Quality control comes before interpretation.

19
00:01:23,276 --> 00:01:31,481
For -V, the first value is the count of nonzero voxels and the second is their volume in cubic millimetres.

20
00:01:31,481 --> 00:01:38,865
A useful self-check is this: Why is F S L stats image -V not automatically a brain-volume measurement?

21
00:01:38,865 --> 00:01:46,250
It counts all nonzero voxels, which may include non-brain signal unless the image is a validated brain mask.

22
00:01:47,100 --> 00:01:51,389
To recap: First, match the utility to the question.

23
00:01:51,389 --> 00:01:54,725
Next, define which voxels a statistic summarizes.

24
00:01:54,725 --> 00:01:58,062
Then, check numerical results against the image.

25
00:01:58,062 --> 00:02:05,687
Before continuing, make sure you can explain this objective: Choose F S L info for metadata.
